{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Too many\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Be careful! That salt is a bit <span class=\\\"strong\\\">too much</span>.<br/>You have drunk <span class=\\\"strong\\\">too much</span> wine!<br/>You are cooking <span class=\\\"strong\\\">too much</span> chicken.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">There are just <span class=\\\"strong\\\">too many</span> cooks in this small kitchen.<br/>There are <span class=\\\"strong\\\">too many</span> ounces of cream!<br/>More than 3 chicken legs is <span class=\\\"strong\\\">too many</span>.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "Oh thanks, Peter, but that's a bit too much.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "There are just too many cooks in this small kitchen.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " You need to do it!", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " \u201c<span class=\"strong\">Have got</span> to\u201d is used to express necessity. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": " \u201c<span class=\"strong\">Have got</span> to\u201d has irregular forms in the past and future. Look at the chart below.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Past\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Future\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I've got  to</span>  start the vindaloo sauce.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I <span class=\\\"italic\\\">  had to</span> start the vindaloo sauce.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" I <span class=\\\"italic\\\">will</span> have to start the vindaloo sauce.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> I've got to</span> put some onions aside.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" I <span class=\\\"italic\\\"> had to</span> put some onions aside.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I <span class=\\\"italic\\\"> will</span> have to put some onions aside.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to put aside", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to save or keep to be used at a later time", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Peter will put aside the extra onions to be used at another time.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le03ob02aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you use to talk about cooking and dining.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "red pepper", "type": "name"}, {"content": " a sweet bell shaped pepper", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The red peppers also need to be saut\u00e9ed before they're added to the curry.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le03ob02aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "tasty", "type": "name"}, {"content": "describing food that tastes good", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Peter thinks Vanessa's cooking is always very tasty.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le03ob02aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to set the table", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to set the place for each person at the dinner table with a fork, knife, glass, etc.", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I can't cook, so I will help set the table.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le03ob02aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to combine", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to put together or to mix", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The last step in making the curry is to combine all the ingredients together.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le03ob02aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "ingredient", "type": "name"}, {"content": "one of the necessary food items or spice in making one dish", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: All of the ingredients have to be prepared right for the dish to taste good.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le03ob02aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Decide with your partner on a meal you both know how to make.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write a dialogue of 12 lines on how to prepare the meal.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write the quantities of the ingredients you need. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write the steps on how to prepare the meal.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Practice the dialogue together. Does it make sense?", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I write a dialogue on how to prepare a meal.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I express quantity on the ingredients we need for a meal.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write the step on how to make a meal.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I make sure the directions make sense.", "type": "text"}]}]}